Hi Uxue,

You are right, the content of the objects is correct, only the formatting is messed up. It is possible that some other packages you are using are interfering with the representation.

The error you get for the calculateDiffMeth is a bit cryptic, but it basically tells you that the methylRaw object is not the correct input object. Also, for running the differential analysis you need more than one sample, and they have to be merged beforehand, as described in the vignette (https://bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/methylKit/inst/doc/methylKit.html#3_Comparative_analysis).

Best,
Alex

